# KEYMAP.md §Global (Normal mode, all Hub screens) [A1] — focus previous / next pane
#
# [A1] is a rule about what is *not* there: `h`/`l`, `Tab`/`S-Tab` and the arrows cycle
# repos ⇄ list and nothing else, and the detail panel is never in the cycle. So the panel is
# opened first (`i`), and then every affordance that moves focus is exercised with it showing:
# `focused` only ever answers `repos.row[N]` or `worktrees.row[N]`, and the ends of the cycle
# clamp instead of wrapping onto a third pane.
fixture: busy
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && hub_pane == List && focused == worktrees.row[0]

# Open the detail panel. It mirrors the cursor row and takes no focus of its own.
key i
await idle
assert focused == worktrees.row[0] && hub_pane == List

# `h` leaves the list for the rail, `l` comes back.
key h
await hub_pane == Repos
assert focused == repos.row[0] && key_contexts[1] == Repos
shot rail-focused
dump rail-focused
key l
await hub_pane == List
assert focused == worktrees.row[0] && key_contexts[1] == Worktrees

# `S-Tab` and `Tab` are the same cycle.
key shift-tab
await hub_pane == Repos
key tab
await hub_pane == List

# The arrows say it once more, and the ends clamp: a second `Tab` from the list has nowhere
# further to go, because the detail panel is not a pane.
key left
await hub_pane == Repos
key right
await hub_pane == List
key tab
await idle
assert hub_pane == List && focused == worktrees.row[0]
key shift-tab
await hub_pane == Repos
key shift-tab
await idle
assert hub_pane == Repos && focused == repos.row[0]
dump clamped
quit
